  level: "Easy",
  q: "A 26-year-old G1P0 at 30 weeks gestation presents with regular uterine contractions and a sensation of pelvic pressure. Vaginal examination reveals the cervix is 3 cm dilated and 80% effaced. Fetal heart tracing is reassuring. Which of the following medications is most appropriate to administer immediately to accelerate fetal lung maturity?",
