  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Intravenous magnesium sulfate):</strong> Magnesium sulfate is given before 32 weeks for fetal *neuroprotection* (reducing the risk of cerebral palsy), but steroids are the specific drug for *lung maturity*.<br>• <strong>Option B (Oral nifedipine):</strong> Nifedipine is a tocolytic used to delay delivery by 48 hours precisely *to allow time* for the corticosteroids to work, but it does not mature the lungs itself.<br>• <strong>Option D (Intravenous indomethacin):</strong> Indomethacin is another tocolytic used before 32 weeks to suppress contractions, not to mature fetal lungs."
