  ans: 1,
  exp: "According to IADPSG/WHO single-step criteria, Gestational Diabetes Mellitus (GDM) is diagnosed if *one or more* values meet/exceed the thresholds: Fasting ≥ 92 mg/dL, 1-hour ≥ 180 mg/dL, 2-hour ≥ 153 mg/dL. This patient's values exceed all three thresholds, confirming GDM. The initial management for GDM is always medical nutrition therapy (dietary modification) and physical exercise. Pharmacotherapy (insulin) is initiated only if target blood sugars are not met after 1-2 weeks of lifestyle intervention.",
