  q: "A 30-year-old primigravida at 34 weeks of gestation complains of severe, intractable itching that is worst at night and primarily involves the palms of her hands and soles of her feet. She has no rash. Laboratory tests show elevated total serum bile acids (45 micromol/L) and slightly elevated AST and ALT. Bilirubin is normal. What is the medication of choice to treat her condition?",
