  exp: "According to the Rotterdam Criteria, a diagnosis of PCOS requires the presence of 2 out of 3 of the following: 1) Oligo/anovulation, 2) Clinical or biochemical hyperandrogenism (hirsutism, acne, elevated testosterone), and 3) Polycystic ovaries on ultrasound. This patient already has oligo-ovulation (irregular cycles) and clinical hyperandrogenism (facial hair, acne), which alone is sufficient to diagnose PCOS, even without the ultrasound findings (which she also happens to have).",
