  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Continuous systemic estrogen monotherapy):</strong> Unopposed systemic estrogen is strictly indicated ONLY for women who have undergone a hysterectomy.<br>• <strong>Option C (Topical vaginal estrogen cream only):</strong> While this is excellent for isolated vaginal atrophy, it does not achieve high enough systemic levels to treat her severe vasomotor symptoms (hot flashes).<br>• <strong>Option D (Oral SSRI):</strong> SSRIs (e.g., paroxetine) can reduce hot flashes and are a good alternative if HRT is contraindicated (e.g., history of breast cancer), but combined HRT is the most effective first-line therapy for severe symptoms."
