  exp: "Adenomyosis is defined by the abnormal presence of endometrial tissue (glands and stroma) deep within the myometrium. It classically presents in multiparous women in their 40s with a triad of heavy menstrual bleeding (menorrhagia), severe dysmenorrhea, and a symmetrically enlarged, globally tender, 'boggy' (soft) uterus on bimanual exam.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Endometriosis):</strong> Characterized by ectopic endometrial tissue outside the uterus. The uterus is typically normal in size or fixed/retroverted, with nodularity along the uterosacral ligaments.<br>• <strong>Option C (Submucosal leiomyoma):</strong> Fibroids cause heavy bleeding, but the uterus is typically irregularly enlarged (lumpy) and firm/hard, not symmetrically globular and boggy.<br>• <strong>Option D (Endometrial carcinoma):</strong> Classically presents as postmenopausal bleeding. The uterus is usually normal size or mildly enlarged, but not typically tender and boggy in a 42-year-old menstruating woman."
