  q: "A 28-year-old woman is prescribed a progestin-only minipill (POP) containing norethindrone for contraception, as she has a history of deep vein thrombosis. She asks how this medication will prevent her from getting pregnant. What is the primary mechanism of action of the traditional progestin-only minipill?",
