  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Repeat Pap smear in 1 year):</strong> This would only be appropriate if the HPV test had been negative (or based on older guidelines). With high-risk HPV present, delaying evaluation is unsafe.<br>• <strong>Option C (LEEP):</strong> LEEP is an excisional treatment procedure indicated for histologically confirmed high-grade dysplasia (CIN II/III), not as a first-line diagnostic step for ASC-US.<br>• <strong>Option D (Cervical conization):</strong> Conization is an excisional procedure used when colposcopy is inadequate (squamocolumnar junction not fully seen) or to treat severe dysplasia/microinvasive cancer, not as the initial step for ASC-US."
