  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option B (Mucinous cystadenocarcinoma):</strong> This is another epithelial tumor but is much less common than serous tumors. It is associated with pseudomyxoma peritonei and huge, multiloculated cysts.<br>• <strong>Option C (Dysgerminoma):</strong> This is a malignant germ cell tumor, which typically presents in adolescents and young women (under 30), not in a 65-year-old. It secretes LDH and hCG.<br>• <strong>Option D (Granulosa cell tumor):</strong> This is a sex cord-stromal tumor that characteristically secretes estrogen, leading to endometrial hyperplasia/bleeding, and has Call-Exner bodies on histology."
