  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Dysgerminoma):</strong> Dysgerminomas are the most common malignant germ cell tumor but have normal AFP. They typically elevate LDH and sometimes hCG. Histology shows 'fried egg' cells with lymphocytic infiltrates.<br>• <strong>Option C (Embryonal carcinoma):</strong> A highly aggressive germ cell tumor that secretes BOTH hCG and AFP, but it does not have Schiller-Duval bodies. Histology shows sheets of undifferentiated cells.<br>• <strong>Option D (Mature cystic teratoma):</strong> Also known as a dermoid cyst, it is benign and composed of mature tissue from all three germ layers (hair, teeth, sebum). It does not elevate AFP/hCG or contain Schiller-Duval bodies."
